text:
 A claim first appends `CLAIM_INTENT`
with status `PREPARED`, writes the claim receipt, then appends `CLAIM_COMMIT`;
install records are appended to the authenticated hash chain.

 Each text file has continuous
byte, codepoint, line, syntax-unit, punctuation, and whitespace/control evidence;
opaque and cached files retain an explicit raw-byte projection.

 Only a real physical mid-swap power
outage receipt, fresh for the final installer, can satisfy that domain;
simulated, mocked, reboot-only, or older-installer evidence cannot.
